# THE LOBBY. The place between rounds (M16).
#
# A CHECKER BAND AT BOTH ENDS, TWO ROWS DEEP EACH. The party is always in a
# corridor between two boundaries; the lobby's own two bands are its entry and
# its exit, so a section is bounded by the exit band of one lobby and the entry
# band of the next. Every rule the round machine has -- both walls, "is everyone
# across", who lived -- is expressed against those two bands and nothing else.
#
# TWO DEEP AND NOT ONE, from the first playtest: one row is 2 m, and four players
# told to stand on it together is four players jostling on a strip narrower than
# they are with the barrier in their faces. Two rows is somewhere to be.
#
# TWELVE ROWS, which is 24 m, of which eight are livable. Long enough that four
# players can spread out and not stand on each other while they pick a hat, short
# enough that walking its length between rounds is a breath rather than a commute.
#
# NO PARAPET SUPPRESSION AND NO HOLES. The lobby is the one place on this bridge
# where falling off is not a design element: the whole point is that it is
# somewhere to stand around. A player who walks off the edge here is a player
# taken away from the thing the lobby is for, and the drone would put them back
# seconds later anyway. It is the only segment in the pool that can say that.
#
# THE RESTOCK. This is where a round is prepared for, so everything a player can
# arrive without is here:
#
#   HEALTH comes back in full, and that is code rather than authoring
#   (game_world._restock_lobby) -- a round is scored on what you carried through
#   it, so arriving on two hit points would let the last round's damage silently
#   decide the next round's score.
#   ONE OF EACH SPECIAL at z4, spread the full width so it reads as a CHOICE
#   rather than a conveyor you walk down collecting all four. You leave with one,
#   because the slot holds one.
#   HATS at z7, four across, past the rack. Hats ARE the score, so how many you
#   can carry out is the question the section asks.
#
# The rack deliberately breaks the rule playtest_bridge.seg states in its own
# header about not opening with a free armoury. A lobby IS the armoury; the cost
# is not scarcity, it is that everything you are carrying is gone the moment you
# fail to reach the next band.

name = lobby
base_height = 0
width = 21
length = 12
tags = foot, lobby, safe

